From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:34:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: apple: take T8132's ANS through a deep sleep

Give T8132's ANS the sleep values T8140's uses. They haven't been traced
on T8132 yet; with them the J713's NVMe comes back from every deep sleep
tested.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2f28e81322bedbddc44e342ecc188f186ba4110d)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index f0892f4986..fb82b04c93 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -3125,6 +3125,11 @@ static const struct apple_nvme_hw apple_nvme_t8132_hw = {
 	.needs_ioq_registers = true,
 	.cold_reset = true,
 	.max_queue_depth = 64,
+	/* T8140's values: T8132's sleep path hasn't been traced. */
+	.sleep_traced = true,
+	.sleep_epmap_last_mask = BIT(0),
+	.sleep_flush_max_nsid = 1,
+	.sleep_shn = NVME_CC_SHN_MASK,
 	/* Explicit flushes are required for writes to survive a reset on J713. */
 	.quirks = NVME_QUIRK_BROKEN_FUA,
 };
